Music Player.text:
{{External|rs}}
[[File:Music tab.png|frame|right|{{mes|Red|color=#ff0000|bg=#332B21|shadow=no}} indicates that the track has not been unlocked.<br/>{{mes|Green|color=#0dc10d|bg=#332B21|shadow=no}} indicates that the track has been unlocked.<br/>{{mes|Grey|color=#9f9f9f|bg=#332B21|shadow=no}} indicates that the track is unavailable to unlock.<br/>{{mes|Blue|color=#3ce6e6|bg=#332B21|shadow=no}} indicates that the track is currently playing.]]
[[File:Music.png|left|The music player interface icon.]]

The '''Music Player''' tab displays what [[music]] track is playing at the moment. Music tracks are unlocked as you play the game, exploring new places and content.

Players can choose between Area Mode, playing a selection of songs for the current area the player is in; Shuffle Mode, playing songs randomly; or Single Mode, playing a chosen song on loop indefinitely. When in Shuffle Mode clicking the Skip Track button will stop playback and start a new randomly chosen song.

By default, track titles in '''green''' have been unlocked by the player, those in '''red''' have not been unlocked (and thus cannot be played), those in '''Grey''' cannot be unlocked and the track title in '''blue''' is the track currently playing. These colours can be configured in the Music Player tab of [[Settings#Music Player|Settings]]. Up to 100 unlocked music tracks can be added to each of the three playlists by right-clicking and selecting "Add to playlist <number>". Playlists can be selected and played from by selecting them from the drop down menu at the top of the music tab.

There are a total of {{Globals|music tracks}} music tracks.

